// Package {{.Module}} owns the module's shared business logic: the
// entities, rules and sentinel errors every surface works with. Surface
// services (internal/modules/{{.Module}}/surfaces/<surface>/service) stay
// thin, audience-specific seams that delegate here, so a rule written once
// serves every surface.
//
// Import direction: http -> service -> {{.Module}} (module root) ->
// repository. The module root never imports a surface package; handlers
// never import the repository package.
//
// Grow this package with plain structs and methods (no framework types):
// the entity views the surfaces map into their DTOs, and the operations the
// surfaces share. Persistence contracts and row structs belong in the
// module-level repository package next door. Wiring (Dependencies and the
// Register<Surface> functions) lives in the surfaces package, keeping this
// package importable from every surface service without a cycle.
package {{.Module}}
